DatAna is a program for the PSION Series 3a to analyse data.

DatAna reads data which is produced with the application data (DBF-files)
and produces as result a table (SPR-file).

In the easiest case DatAna is a transformation program which
transforms DBF-files to SPR-files.

More over you may select only some records, skip over fields and
define data types or field parts for some fields.

You may count data records or cumulate numerical data (sum, average,
minimum, maximum). There are one- or two-dimensional conversions
available.

The parameters of a conversion may be saved to repeat them after
the data in the DBF-file has been updated.

After the installation read the tutorial in the file DATANA.WRD.

There is also a German version of DatAna. The generated files
are independent of the language version.

Installation:

The following files belong to DatAna:

	datana.opa	-	application program
	datana.rsc	-	help text
	install.bat	-	installation procedure for RCOM
	datana.dbf	-	example of a DBF-file
	datana.wrd	-	introduction text
	datana.txt	-	ASCII version of introduction text
	tutor?.d2s	-	example conversions
	uninstal.bat	-	un-installation procedure
	read.me 	-	this text
	
MINIMAL INSTALLATION:
    
It is sufficient to copy just DATANA.OPA to a directory \APP and to
install it from the system screen.

Optionally you can copy the help file DATANA.RSC to a directory \OPD.

INSTALLATION with RCOM:

With 
	RCOM INSTALL <drive:>
*all* files are copied to the PSION:	     

	datana.opa	in	\APP\
	datana.rsc	in	\OPD\
	datana.dbf	in	i:\DAT\
	datana.wrd	in	\WRD\
	tutor?.d2s	in	\D2S\

After that you have to install from the system screen DatAna
with PSION-i.

With				 
	RCOM UNINSTAL <drive:>
*all* files belonging to DatAna are deleted from the PSION.
	
MANUAL INSTALLATION:

Create a directory \D2S\ on your internal drive and copy 
the files to right directories as shown under "Installation 
with RCOM" to your PSION.

You may use any drive (M: A: B:). The file DATANA.DBF *MUST*
go to the the internal drive in directory \D2S.

